═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§ THEORETICAL-NOTES ← §§ T21-depth-hints
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  SSA construction :
    naive : pre-process to eliminate all assignments
    Braun et al. 2013 : "Simple and Efficient Construction of SSA Form"
      on-the-fly • no dominance-tree needed
      recommend ∵ matches our walk-based lowering
    Cytron et al. 1991 : dominance-frontier classic
      needs control-flow-graph explicit
      overkill for structured-IR
  structured-regions :
    MLIR-pattern : ops-with-regions • Op owns Region[]
    Thorin IR : higher-order functional • no-blocks
      elegant but non-standard
    RVSDG : regions as first-class
      good for analysis • more complex to emit
    recommend MLIR-pattern ∵ SPIR-V-compatible (future CSSLv3-interop)
  phi-nodes vs block-args :
    phi : classical Cytron-style • per-value at merge-points
    block-args : Cranelift/MLIR-style • cleaner semantics
    recommend block-args ∵ structured-CFG has-few merge-points
  verifier design :
    bottom-up : verify ops after-their-operands
    top-down : verify containers before-contents (regions before ops)
    hybrid : recommend ← structural-first, then op-types
  error-recovery in lowering :
    fail-fast : first-error stops lowering
    accumulate : collect all errors • emit all
    recommend accumulate ∵ better-diagnostics • matches parser-pattern

